  user_input {
    user_response: "Act as an Expert Frontend Developer. Build a complete, interactive single-file React prototype (using Tailwind CSS and Lucide React icons) for a product showcase of an accessible HireVue alternative that translates American Sign Language (ASL) to text for mute and Deaf candidates.\n\nBecause this is strictly a showcase demo and the presenter does not know ASL, implement a streamlined, linear 2-step user flow with built-in sample ASL video inputs and no backend dependencies:\n\n### 1. The 3 Hardcoded Interview Questions\nLock the interview flow to these exact 3 questions in sequence:\n- **Question 1:** \"Tell us about a complex project you led and how you handled team communication.\"\n- **Question 2:** \"Describe a time you had to resolve a conflict or misalignment under a tight deadline.\"\n- **Question 3:** \"Why are you excited about this role, and what unique perspective do you bring?\"\n\n### 2. Step 1: The Candidate Recording & Live ASL Transcription Studio\n- **Input Source Toggle (\"Live Webcam\" vs. \"Load Hardcoded ASL Sample Video\"):**\n  - Include a prominent button/toggle in the video control bar: **\"Use Pre-Recorded ASL Sample Video\"**.\n  - When clicked, instead of the presenter\'s webcam, load a realistic simulated ASL signer video/canvas animation (complete with animated 21-point MediaPipe hand-tracking skeletal landmarks, bounding boxes, and finger-joint vectors moving in sync with the signing) tailored to the current question.\n  - Also keep the option to switch back to the presenter\'s live HTML5 webcam feed with the HUD overlay.\n- **3-Question Stepper:** Show a visual progress bar for Questions 1, 2, and 3.\n- **Synchronized Real-Time ASL-to-Text Pipeline:** When the user clicks \"Start Recording\" (or \"Play & Translate ASL Sample\"):\n  1. **Raw ASL Gloss Ticker:** Animate detected ASL sign tokens appearing in real-time synchronized with the video playback (e.g., for Q1: `[PAST] -> [PROJECT-COMPLEX] -> [ME-LEAD] -> [TEAM] -> [VISUAL-BOARD] -> [SUCCESS]`).\n  2. **Natural English Live Transcript:** Dynamically stream the LLM-translated, grammatically complete English sentences into a live transcript box below the video as the sample video plays.\n- **Review & Next:** Allow the user to stop the recording/sample, optionally edit the captured transcript for that question, and click \"Save & Next Question\" (or \"Submit Interview\" after Question 3).\n\n### 3. Step 2: The AI Candidate Judgment & Evaluation Dashboard (Post-Submission)\nImmediately after Question 3 is submitted, transition to a polished \"Recruiter AI Evaluation & Judgment\" screen for the fictional candidate (\"Alex Rivera - Senior Product Designer\") that displays:\n- **Overall Hire Recommendation Badge:** (e.g., \"94% Match \342\200\224 Strong Hire\") with an \"ASL Accessibility Mode Verified (Bias-Adjusted)\" tag explaining that vocal tone, speech cadence, and standard eye-contact penalties were automatically replaced with linguistic content analysis.\n- **Competency Scorecard:** Visual progress bars and scores (out of 10) for *Technical Depth*, *Problem Solving*, *Leadership*, and *Clarity of Thought*, with a short AI-generated justification for each.\n- **Question-by-Question Breakdown:** Cards for each of the 3 hardcoded questions showing:\n  - A replayable thumbnail of the hardcoded ASL sample video used for that question.\n  - The final translated English transcript alongside the raw ASL Gloss tokens.\n  - **AI Judgment Note:** A specific critique of why the candidate\'s answer to that question scored high (e.g., \"Strong STAR method structure; demonstrated proactive stakeholder alignment\").\n- **Reset Demo Button:** A button in the header to reset the flow back to Question 1 for the next showcase viewer."
    items {
      text: "Act as an Expert Frontend Developer. Build a complete, interactive single-file React prototype (using Tailwind CSS and Lucide React icons) for a product showcase of an accessible HireVue alternative that translates American Sign Language (ASL) to text for mute and Deaf candidates.\n\nBecause this is strictly a showcase demo and the presenter does not know ASL, implement a streamlined, linear 2-step user flow with built-in sample ASL video inputs and no backend dependencies:\n\n### 1. The 3 Hardcoded Interview Questions\nLock the interview flow to these exact 3 questions in sequence:\n- **Question 1:** \"Tell us about a complex project you led and how you handled team communication.\"\n- **Question 2:** \"Describe a time you had to resolve a conflict or misalignment under a tight deadline.\"\n- **Question 3:** \"Why are you excited about this role, and what unique perspective do you bring?\"\n\n### 2. Step 1: The Candidate Recording & Live ASL Transcription Studio\n- **Input Source Toggle (\"Live Webcam\" vs. \"Load Hardcoded ASL Sample Video\"):**\n  - Include a prominent button/toggle in the video control bar: **\"Use Pre-Recorded ASL Sample Video\"**.\n  - When clicked, instead of the presenter\'s webcam, load a realistic simulated ASL signer video/canvas animation (complete with animated 21-point MediaPipe hand-tracking skeletal landmarks, bounding boxes, and finger-joint vectors moving in sync with the signing) tailored to the current question.\n  - Also keep the option to switch back to the presenter\'s live HTML5 webcam feed with the HUD overlay.\n- **3-Question Stepper:** Show a visual progress bar for Questions 1, 2, and 3.\n- **Synchronized Real-Time ASL-to-Text Pipeline:** When the user clicks \"Start Recording\" (or \"Play & Translate ASL Sample\"):\n  1. **Raw ASL Gloss Ticker:** Animate detected ASL sign tokens appearing in real-time synchronized with the video playback (e.g., for Q1: `[PAST] -> [PROJECT-COMPLEX] -> [ME-LEAD] -> [TEAM] -> [VISUAL-BOARD] -> [SUCCESS]`).\n  2. **Natural English Live Transcript:** Dynamically stream the LLM-translated, grammatically complete English sentences into a live transcript box below the video as the sample video plays.\n- **Review & Next:** Allow the user to stop the recording/sample, optionally edit the captured transcript for that question, and click \"Save & Next Question\" (or \"Submit Interview\" after Question 3).\n\n### 3. Step 2: The AI Candidate Judgment & Evaluation Dashboard (Post-Submission)\nImmediately after Question 3 is submitted, transition to a polished \"Recruiter AI Evaluation & Judgment\" screen for the fictional candidate (\"Alex Rivera - Senior Product Designer\") that displays:\n- **Overall Hire Recommendation Badge:** (e.g., \"94% Match \342\200\224 Strong Hire\") with an \"ASL Accessibility Mode Verified (Bias-Adjusted)\" tag explaining that vocal tone, speech cadence, and standard eye-contact penalties were automatically replaced with linguistic content analysis.\n- **Competency Scorecard:** Visual progress bars and scores (out of 10) for *Technical Depth*, *Problem Solving*, *Leadership*, and *Clarity of Thought*, with a short AI-generated justification for each.\n- **Question-by-Question Breakdown:** Cards for each of the 3 hardcoded questions showing:\n  - A replayable thumbnail of the hardcoded ASL sample video used for that question.\n  - The final translated English transcript alongside the raw ASL Gloss tokens.\n  - **AI Judgment Note:** A specific critique of why the candidate\'s answer to that question scored high (e.g., \"Strong STAR method structure; demonstrated proactive stakeholder alignment\").\n- **Reset Demo Button:** A button in the header to reset the flow back to Question 1 for the next showcase viewer."
    }
  }
}
