  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s request. My focus is now on the core problem: creating an accessible, real-time ASL-to-text translator for job interviews, specifically tailored for a demo scenario where the presenter *doesn\'t* know sign language. The \"SignVue\" / \"AuraASL\" / \"SignVoice Interview\" concept is taking shape as a potential product name framework.\n\n\n**Defining the Core Functionality**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a focused, 2-step user flow. The goal is a straightforward experience. I\'ve defined three hardcoded interview questions, serving as the basis. The first step involves a \"Live ASL Transcription Studio\" with an input source toggle. Users can choose between a live webcam or hardcoded sample videos featuring animated 21-point hand tracking. These videos, tailored to each interview question, will provide a realistic simulation.\n\n\n**Refining the Transcription Pipeline**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the real-time ASL-to-text pipeline. My approach includes a webcam feed using `getUserMedia` with landmark tracking. A three-question stepper and a real-time synchronized pipeline are planned. This will feature raw ASL gloss tokens updating with sample video playback. Simultaneously, an LLM will translate into a live English transcript. I also envision allowing users to review and edit each question\'s transcript before moving on.\n\n\n**Designing the Final Screens**\n\nI\'m now designing the final screens for the demo. I\'ve conceptualized a \"Recruiter AI Evaluation & Judgment\" screen, immediately following question submission. This screen will feature an overall hire recommendation with an accessibility tag, a competency scorecard with justifications, and a breakdown of each question with replayable ASL samples, transcripts, gloss tokens, and AI judgment notes. A reset button will be added to the header, too.\n\n\n**Generating Candidate Avatars**\n\nI\'m now focusing on generating images. I\'ve decided to create two images to elevate the experience. The first is a candidate avatar for Alex Rivera, a Senior Product Designer. The second will be a reference image of an ASL signer for the simulated video background. I\'ll execute the `generate_image` calls in a single batch as part of the Phase 1 generation, as well.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_303911"
      name: "view_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"AbsolutePath\":\"/metadata.json\",\"toolAction\":\"Viewing metadata.json\",\"toolSummary\":\"Check current metadata.json\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "view_file"
    }
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 906834525
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    provider_assigned_message_id: "e6TOauDQIIXrqtsP1IPr2Q8"
  }
}
