    thinking: "**Analyzing Interview Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the user prompt\'s requirements. Right now, I\'m focused on the hardcoded interview questions. I\'ve successfully identified and listed the first two questions, along with their prompts. Next, I\'ll identify any other requirements specified by the user.\n\n\n**Defining Role Excitement**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the third interview question: \"Why are you excited about this role, and what unique perspective do you bring?\" I\'m now analyzing its core concepts to get prepared for crafting a response. I\'m focusing on \"excitement\" and \"unique perspective\" \342\200\223 key elements that need careful consideration.\n\n\n**Visualizing Workflow Details**\n\nI\'m now outlining the user interface elements. I\'m focusing on the 3-question stepper visual, its progress indicators, and the real-time ASL-to-text pipeline. I\'m visualizing the \"Start Recording\" button and how it launches the video, the animation, and the raw ASL gloss ticker, all synchronized and in real-time. The idea is to have a dynamic display reflecting the ASL sign tokens as the video plays.\n\n\n**Mapping Product Development Path**\n\nI\'m now charting the development path, focusing on the order and dependencies of each element. First, I have to ensure accessibility standards are met and understand the need for user data sharing. This also includes the necessity of reaching a consensus. My goal is to eventually ship the product.\n\nI\'ve also moved on to Q3, I\'m thinking about the concepts of excited about joining the company for its mission of inclusion, and bringing my perspective as a Deaf designer to bring an accessible-first mindset which will lead to innovation and contribute impact. I am thinking of including sentence-by-sentence streaming animations with live transcripts.\n\n\n**Refining Approach Details**\n\nI\'m now refining Q2, and I\'m detailing the accessibility conflict from the Q3 launch, and the resolution which included user testing and design compromise, to meet the goal to ship on time. I\'m now crafting a response for Q3; I\'m highlighting my seven years of expertise in inclusive interface architecture and emphasizing accessibility as my core daily experience. I\'m focusing on bringing expertise in universal design systems, multimodality, and gesture-driven UX. I\'m preparing to outline how I want to help this team create products that are universally intuitive. Finally, I\'m noting the user can stop recording, and review it.\n\n\n**Designing UI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user interface details after the recording. I envision an editable text area for directly modifying the transcript. There will also be a \"Save & Next Question\" button to navigate through the questions. And finally, on Question 3, there will be a \"Submit Interview & Generate AI Evaluation\" button.\n\n\n**Evaluating Interview Analysis**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a more granular breakdown. I\'m imagining interactive cards for each of the three questions, each including the ASL sample, the English transcript, and the raw ASL gloss. I\'m also considering including AI judgment notes explaining the candidate\'s high score. Finally, I\'m thinking of interactive dashboard capabilities, such as a replay button and the ability to toggle \"Standard AI Hiring\" vs. \"Advanced DEI AI Hiring.\"\n\n\n**Defining UI/UX Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the final interface elements. I\'m visualizing the difference between a standard AI hiring algorithm versus the \"SignVue Bias-Adjusted Algorithm,\" showcasing how it dramatically improves the candidate\'s score. I\'m imagining a printable summary, and a reset button to restart the process for a new user. The design avoids generic AI cliches, aiming for clean unboxed metadata and tabular numerals.\n\n\n**Visualizing Hands and UI**\n\nI\'m now diving into the hand tracking simulation for the UI. I\'m focusing on rendering the 21-point hand skeleton on an HTML5 canvas, using glowing cyan and amber joints and bones. I\'m also planning to incorporate bounding boxes with confidence scores for each hand, and simulate realistic hand movements based on ASL signs. I\'m also thinking of face mesh landmarks to show non-manual facial markers.\n\n```\nsrc/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/         # Reusable UI components\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/           # Backend data\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 utils/              # Helper functions\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 App.js              # Entry point\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 index.js            # Entry point\n```\n\n\n**Defining File Structure**\n\nI\'m now focusing on file organization. I\'ve begun defining the `src/` directory structure, with key components, services, and utilities. I\'ve outlined data types for questions and evaluations, and data for ASL timelines, transcripts, and AI notes. Furthermore, I\'ve started building the canvas simulation engine for hand tracking.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_395733"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export interface GlossToken {\\n  timeMs: number;\\n  token: string;\\n  meaning: string;\\n  confidence: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface QuestionData {\\n  id: number;\\n  numberText: string;\\n  question: string;\\n  context: string;\\n  suggestedDurationSec: number;\\n  glossSequence: GlossToken[];\\n  sampleEnglishTranscript: string;\\n  aiJudgmentNote: string;\\n  competencyHighlights: string[];\\n  sampleGestures: {\\n    startMs: number;\\n    endMs: number;\\n    primaryHand: \'left\' | \'right\' | \'both\';\\n    handshape: \'open5\' | \'fist\' | \'pointing\' | \'flatB\' | \'vShape\';\\n    motion: \'chestSweep\' | \'forwardPush\' | \'circular\' | \'horizontalWave\' | \'nodding\';\\n  }[];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface CompetencyScore {\\n  name: string;\\n  score: number; // out of 10\\n  maxScore: number;\\n  justification: string;\\n  trend: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface CandidateProfile {\\n  name: string;\\n  role: string;\\n  experience: string;\\n  matchScore: number;\\n  recommendation: \'Strong Hire\' | \'Hire\' | \'Review\';\\n  accessibilityVerified: boolean;\\n  avatarSeed: string;\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Define types for questions, ASL glosses, candidate profiles, and evaluation scores\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/types/interview.ts\",\"toolAction\":\"Writing interview types\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create interview types file\"}"
