  planner_response {
    response: "I have built a complete, interactive, zero-dependency prototype for **SignVue**, an accessible HireVue alternative designed for Deaf and mute candidates using American Sign Language (ASL).\n\n### What Was Built\n\n1. **The 3 Hardcoded Interview Questions (Locked Sequence)**\n   - **Question 1:** *\"Tell us about a complex project you led and how you handled team communication.\"*\n   - **Question 2:** *\"Describe a time you had to resolve a conflict or misalignment under a tight deadline.\"*\n   - **Question 3:** *\"Why are you excited about this role, and what unique perspective do you bring?\"*\n\n2. **Step 1: Candidate Recording & Live ASL Transcription Studio**\n   - **Input Source Toggle:** Prominently toggle between **\"ASL Sample Video\"** and **\"Live Webcam\"**.\n   - **MediaPipe Hand-Tracking Simulation:** Realistic 21-point dual-hand skeletal tracking engine (wrist, MCP, PIP, DIP, TIP finger joints) complete with color-coded bounding boxes, confidence telemetry (`99.4%`), facial mesh anchors for non-manual grammatical signals, and gesture kinematics synchronized to each question.\n   - **Visual 3-Question Stepper:** Displays active, completed, and upcoming questions with duration tracking and timecode counters.\n   - **Synchronized Real-Time ASL-to-Text Pipeline:**\n     - **Raw ASL Gloss Ticker:** Streams detected ASL sign tokens with confidence ratings (e.g. `[PAST] \342\206\222 [PROJECT-COMPLEX] \342\206\222 [ME-LEAD] \342\206\222 [FOUR-TEAM-CROSS] \342\206\222 [MAKE-VISUAL-BOARD] \342\206\222 [SUCCESS]`).\n     - **Natural English Live Transcript:** Dynamically streams the grammatically complete, synthesized English sentences in real time.\n   - **Review & Adjust:** Includes an inline transcript editor, play/pause controls, a **Showcase Instant Fill** fast-forward button for quick demonstrations, and a *\"Save & Next Question\"* workflow.\n\n3. **Step 2: AI Candidate Judgment & Evaluation Dashboard**\n   - **Candidate Dossier for Alex Rivera (Senior Product Designer):**\n     - **Overall Hire Recommendation Badge:** `94% Match \342\200\224 Strong Hire` with the **ASL Accessibility Mode Verified (Bias-Adjusted)** tag explaining that vocal tone, acoustic pitch, and eye-contact penalties were removed in favor of 3D spatial sign structure and linguistic substance.\n     - **Competency Scorecard:** Scores and progress bars for *Technical Depth* (9.6/10), *Problem Solving* (9.3/10), *Leadership* (9.5/10), and *Clarity of Thought* (9.2/10) with AI justifications.\n     - **Algorithmic Fairness Comparison:** Live comparison toggle demonstrating how standard legacy AI unfairly penalizes deaf candidates (dropping them to 41%) versus SignVue\'s equitable score.\n     - **Question-by-Question Breakdown:** Individual cards with replayable ASL video thumbnails, synchronized modal replayers, translated transcripts, raw gloss tokens, and AI critique notes.\n   - **Reset Demo Button:** Positioned in the header to restart the showcase from Question 1 anytime."
    thinking: "**Verifying Project Requirements**\n\nOkay, so I\'ve confirmed that both the `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` processes ran without a hitch, producing zero errors. Now, I\'m meticulously checking the prompt\'s requirements to ensure total compliance. The first requirement, the hardcoded interview question regarding team communication, is definitely included in the current configuration.\n\n\n**Confirming Functionality of Module**\n\nI have now ensured the inclusion of the final two interview questions. Furthermore, I\'ve confirmed that the \'Use Pre-Recorded ASL Sample Video\' option is prominent in the control bar. I\'m now also thinking about the animated hand tracking and how it\'ll render and move as the signer signs. Finally, the design of the visual progress bar has been implemented to display each questions\' status as the user goes through the app.\n\n\n**Analyzing AI Candidate Evaluation**\n\nI\'m now diving into the AI candidate judgment and evaluation dashboard. My primary focus is on the design and function of the hire recommendation badge and the competency scorecard. I\'m considering how best to visually represent competency scores and provide clear, concise justifications. Specifically, how the \"ASL Accessibility Mode Verified\" tag factors into the final recommendation.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have built a complete, interactive, zero-dependency prototype for **SignVue**, an accessible HireVue alternative designed for Deaf and mute candidates using American Sign Language (ASL).\n\n### What Was Built\n\n1. **The 3 Hardcoded Interview Questions (Locked Sequence)**\n   - **Question 1:** *\"Tell us about a complex project you led and how you handled team communication.\"*\n   - **Question 2:** *\"Describe a time you had to resolve a conflict or misalignment under a tight deadline.\"*\n   - **Question 3:** *\"Why are you excited about this role, and what unique perspective do you bring?\"*\n\n2. **Step 1: Candidate Recording & Live ASL Transcription Studio**\n   - **Input Source Toggle:** Prominently toggle between **\"ASL Sample Video\"** and **\"Live Webcam\"**.\n   - **MediaPipe Hand-Tracking Simulation:** Realistic 21-point dual-hand skeletal tracking engine (wrist, MCP, PIP, DIP, TIP finger joints) complete with color-coded bounding boxes, confidence telemetry (`99.4%`), facial mesh anchors for non-manual grammatical signals, and gesture kinematics synchronized to each question.\n   - **Visual 3-Question Stepper:** Displays active, completed, and upcoming questions with duration tracking and timecode counters.\n   - **Synchronized Real-Time ASL-to-Text Pipeline:**\n     - **Raw ASL Gloss Ticker:** Streams detected ASL sign tokens with confidence ratings (e.g. `[PAST] \342\206\222 [PROJECT-COMPLEX] \342\206\222 [ME-LEAD] \342\206\222 [FOUR-TEAM-CROSS] \342\206\222 [MAKE-VISUAL-BOARD] \342\206\222 [SUCCESS]`).\n     - **Natural English Live Transcript:** Dynamically streams the grammatically complete, synthesized English sentences in real time.\n   - **Review & Adjust:** Includes an inline transcript editor, play/pause controls, a **Showcase Instant Fill** fast-forward button for quick demonstrations, and a *\"Save & Next Question\"* workflow.\n\n3. **Step 2: AI Candidate Judgment & Evaluation Dashboard**\n   - **Candidate Dossier for Alex Rivera (Senior Product Designer):**\n     - **Overall Hire Recommendation Badge:** `94% Match \342\200\224 Strong Hire` with the **ASL Accessibility Mode Verified (Bias-Adjusted)** tag explaining that vocal tone, acoustic pitch, and eye-contact penalties were removed in favor of 3D spatial sign structure and linguistic substance.\n     - **Competency Scorecard:** Scores and progress bars for *Technical Depth* (9.6/10), *Problem Solving* (9.3/10), *Leadership* (9.5/10), and *Clarity of Thought* (9.2/10) with AI justifications.\n     - **Algorithmic Fairness Comparison:** Live comparison toggle demonstrating how standard legacy AI unfairly penalizes deaf candidates (dropping them to 41%) versus SignVue\'s equitable score.\n     - **Question-by-Question Breakdown:** Individual cards with replayable ASL video thumbnails, synchronized modal replayers, translated transcripts, raw gloss tokens, and AI critique notes.\n   - **Reset Demo Button:** Positioned in the header to restart the showcase from Question 1 anytime."
