  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining ASL Accuracy**\n\nI\'m currently focused on enhancing the American Sign Language (ASL) demo\'s authenticity. I\'m exploring how to improve both the linguistic and anatomical accuracy of the signs. My efforts center around making the sign production much more realistic, paying close attention to the details.\n\n\n**Analyzing ASL Parameters**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the five crucial phonological parameters of ASL: handshape, palm orientation, location, movement, and non-manual markers. I\'m aiming to integrate these elements to produce more authentic and nuanced sign representations. I\'m particularly interested in realistically rendering the signer\'s appearance in the visualizer.\n\n\n**Developing Realistic ASL Signs**\n\nI\'m now implementing anatomically accurate hand representations for specific ASL signs. I\'m focusing on reproducing complex handshapes for signs like \"PAST,\" \"LEAD,\" \"TEAM,\" \"COMMUNICATE,\" \"PROBLEM,\" \"DESIGN,\" and \"SUCCESS.\" The goal is enhanced realism with detailed MediaPipe Holistic tracking overlays, including precise color aesthetics, joint radius sizing, and bone connections to visualize motions. I\'m also including velocity vectors on moving joints and confidence scores. Upper-body pose landmarks are also implemented.\n\n\n**Integrating ASL Facial Grammar**\n\nI\'m now integrating non-manual markers and facial grammar, using MediaPipe FaceMesh to capture nuanced expressions. I\'m focusing on authentic ASL gloss notation, including topic-comment structure and classifier predicates, to render accurate visual representations. I\'m leveraging real-time kinematic telemetry and spatial signing quadrants for enhanced realism. The upper-body pose landmarks are also implemented.\n\n\n**Visualizing ASL Grammar**\n\nI\'m now focusing on displaying authentic ASL grammatical tiers. I\'m prioritizing Non-Manual Markers (NMM), primary ASL glosses, 3D spatial loci indexing, and synthesized English translations. I\'m ensuring all information is correctly rendered in order, to make the display more intuitive and useful.\n\n\n**Enhancing Linguistic Realism**\n\nI\'m now integrating real ASL linguistic parameters into the visualizer. I\'m adding a panel displaying the handshape name, palm orientation, movement type, and non-manual markers in real time. Also, I\'m developing an interactive signing practice mode with a webcam test and calibration guide for users. I\'m refining the realism of the transcript by including linguistic justifications for ASL\'s distinct morphology and grammar.\n\n\n"
